      "footnote": "Data on research and development (R&D) in Singapore are collected through the National Survey of Research, Innovation and Enterprise (RIE), conducted on an annual basis by the Agency for Science, Technology and Research (A*STAR).  The institutional sectors in the RIE Survey are broadly split into three sectors, namely (a) 'Private sector' comprises all business enterprises, excluding institutions of higher learning; (b) 'Government sector' comprises all government organisations, including government ministries, statutory boards & public research institutes and excluding institutes of higher learning; and (c) 'Institutes of Higher Learning' comprises institutions of higher learning, including the universities and polytechnics.  For detailed definitions for areas of research, please refer to 'Section 7. Explanatory Notes and Definitions' of the publication 'National Survey of Research, Innovation and Enterprise (RIE)' at https://www.a-star.edu.sg/News/national-survey-of-rie",
